# Phase 18 signed RPC timeout connection-order gate

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 03:16:08 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`
- Implementation commit: `76cdc31a161c22bcbd849ec5d295c25ec9e726e2`

## Finding and change

Pinned Java `NettyRemotingClient.invokeSync` records the call start time, calls
`getAndCreateChannel`, and only then subtracts the elapsed milliseconds from
the signed timeout. When the remaining budget is zero or negative, it throws
before calling `invokeSyncImpl`, so it may establish a TCP channel but does not
send a Broker request frame. `MQClientInstance.queryAssignment` forwards its
signed timeout to `MQClientAPIImpl.queryAssignment`; consumer-list lookup uses
the live signed `mqClientApiTimeout` setting.

The Rust runtime previously converted non-positive values to an already-expired
deadline. Its transport returned before acquiring a channel, which skipped the
Java connection side effect. The new signed-millisecond invocation path first
acquires or creates the connection, subtracts elapsed whole milliseconds, then
either returns timeout without sending or continues with the remaining budget.
Both runtime lookup methods now use this path. Consumer-list errors remain
best-effort and return `None`; assignment errors remain propagated.

## Verification

- `cargo test --offline -p rocketmq-classic-core --test runtime_lookup` — passed
  (17 tests). The timeout regression covers Java fixture values `0` and `-1`,
  confirms a Broker socket is established with no request bytes, and checks a
  negative live consumer timeout also emits no frame and is swallowed.
- `cargo clippy --offline -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` — passed.
- `cargo fmt --all` and `cargo fmt --all --check` — passed.
- `git diff --check` — passed before the implementation commit.
- Pinned source review: `NettyRemotingClient.invokeSync` lines 556–569;
  `MQClientInstance.queryAssignment` lines 1373–1384; and
  `MQClientAPIImpl.queryAssignment` lines 405–420;
  `MQClientInstance.findConsumerIdList` lines 1355–1367; and
  `MQClientAPIImpl.getConsumerIdListByGroup` lines 1435–1445.

## Scope and remaining evidence

This closes the signed timeout/channel-acquisition ordering slice for the two
runtime lookups. It does not close broad P18-V01 source/API/settings/input/error
and reverse-export reconciliation. Current-revision remote Ubuntu CI, native
Windows runtime evidence, and Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation remain open.
No external Java checkout or Phase 19 file was changed; no remote CI or live
Broker was used.
